  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a differentiable function such that <math><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></math>, (where,&nbsp;<math><mi>C</mi></math> is the constant of integration) and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> equals",
    "image": null
  },
